Subject: [PATCH 11137/11171] [outer-loop] Correction: the flag-ledger bug hit
 18 flags and predated my edits

Commit 3f54902081 claims the flag_states defect was latent and that recording
the authorized nulls exposed it. Wrong, and measured rather than reasoned:
running the old regex against the ledger as it stood before tonight's edits
returns 18 of 136 flags reading '?', and exactly the same 18 afterwards. Both
flags I recorded were already in that set.

So 13 percent of the ledger had been unreadable by state for an unknown
period, not two entries. It surfaced now only because the dashboard watches
four flags and two of the eighteen are among them; the other fourteen were
broken and off-screen. The visible symptom was a sampling accident, not the
extent of the fault.

I inferred 'latent, exposed by my edit' from the sequence without running the
old code against the old file. That is the correlation-without-a-base-rate
error this session has a standing instruction about, committed inside a commit
message. One command settled it.

The earlier message stands unedited per never-prune; this is the correction.

